{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bit felt useful because making different-sized mounting holes connects with my recent drywall anchors and screws.",
    "That drill bit recognized a possible next step in my mounting work: preparing holes for the fasteners I have been buying."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Rivet nuts and machine screws look related to my fastener purchases, but they serve different jobs from the wood and drywall fastening I have needed.",
    "Replacement bags suggest I am maintaining an existing vacuum; they do not give me a reason to buy a new vacuum mop or spray mop.",
    "Electrical tape, indicator lights, precision calipers, and a thread checker require specific needs I have not shown, while the rapid test does not fit my current shopping purpose."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying nails and screws seems to have been treated as interest in almost any hardware or workshop supply.",
    "Buying vacuum bags seems to have been treated as interest in cleaning equipment generally."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The materials and fastening methods matter: my recent purchases center on framing, wood, and drywall, rather than threaded metal assemblies.",
    "I choose supplies for a concrete task. A potentially useful accessory needs a clear connection to that task, rather than simply belonging in a toolbox.",
    "Replacement purchases can mean I want to keep using equipment I already own, especially when the replacement specifies compatible vacuum types."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions partly recognized my mounting work but stretched that interest into unrelated hardware and treated vacuum maintenance as a need for new cleaning equipment."
}"}
